The bundler does detect them. If we keep the wrapping `if`, it will transpile to something like:

```js
// ...
{
  // whatever was here on top on the warning
}
// ...
```

With the condition inside the `warning` method, it's completely stripped.

FYI this is what React is doing for their [`invariant`](https://github.com/facebook/react/blob/master/packages/shared/invariant.js) and [`warning`](https://github.com/facebook/react/blob/master/packages/shared/warning.js) functions.
